<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Arab-Byzantine Condominium of Cyprus</h1><p class="st-meta">688 CE – 965 CE (approx.) · capital Constantia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nearly three centuries in which Cyprus was neutral ground shared between the Byzantine Empire and the Caliphate, which split its taxes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Arab fleets raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> from 649. In 688 the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii">Justinian II</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-malik-ibn-marwan">Abd al-Malik</a> agreed a treaty under which the revenues of Cyprus, along with those of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, were divided equally between them. The island was to be demilitarised and neutral, though the arrangement was repeatedly interrupted.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> kept its Greek-speaking Christian population, its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and local officials, while paying tribute to both powers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii">Justinian II</a> moved many islanders to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cyzicus">Cyzicus</a> around 691, and they returned about 698. Both sides violated the neutrality: Byzantine and Abbasid fleets raided the island, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid's</a> forces deported Cypriots. Historians debate how formal the condominium really was.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As Byzantine power revived in the 10th century, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a> sent the patrician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niketas-chalkoutzes">Niketas Chalkoutzes</a> to retake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> in 965. It became a Byzantine province until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-komnenos-of-cyprus">Isaac Komnenos</a> seized it in 1184.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 688 CE – 965 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:73.39%;width:5.51%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>688 CE – 965 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Constantia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity, Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Medieval Greek, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cyprus">Cyprus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cypriot condominium, Cyprus condominium</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=826&amp;focus=arab-byzantine-condominium-of-cyprus" aria-label="Arab-Byzantine Condominium of Cyprus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5519 914 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Arab-Byzantine Condominium of Cyprus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M6134 1224h0M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5839 1170h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5839 1170h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Cyprus. <a href="/atlas?year=826&amp;focus=arab-byzantine-condominium-of-cyprus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

